  "body": "### What problem are you trying to solve?\n\nThe `change` event fires too late. Authors that want to respond to changes _before_ the change is actually committed can’t do so, because the change was already committed when `change` has fired.\r\n\r\nSee https://codepen.io/bramus/pen/xxmozvN for example which starts a View Transition when the selected radio button changes. Because `change` fires too late, I had to listen to the `click` event to respond to the selected value changing. This feels wrong.\n\n### What solutions exist today?\n\nUse a different event, such as `click` (radio buttons) or `keydown` (text inputs) or something else, depending on which events the input fires.\n\n### How would you solve it?\n\nBy having a generic `beforechange` event availble, one would have a uniform approach to hooking into this.\n\n### Anything else?\n\nThere already is `beforetoggle` for components that fire `toggle` events.",
